                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc57469f-a744-4071-a826-e6761d300041",
                                                "sense_id": "8e533f97-7538-3788-ad2b-bf321ae80472",
                                                "text": "To switch off the instrument when the clockwork is not wound up, and to remind the subscriber of doing so, there is provided an indicator, x, which is worked in the following manner."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2f3d338-7a2e-4f87-a352-daec94c858f3",
                                                "sense_id": "8e533f97-7538-3788-ad2b-bf321ae80472",
                                                "text": "We have found that a patrolman in the central section of the city can switch on, and later switch off, 100 signs with ease."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "409fcfee-c867-4b81-8cb8-ad38eff1bd66",
                                                "sense_id": "8e533f97-7538-3788-ad2b-bf321ae80472",
                                                "text": "He began shutting down the flight controls, switching off all the things he'd switched on before, switching on all the things he'd switched off."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78ef8052-df61-3a23-9c1b-f71536b80397",
                                        "entry_id": "a0eec63c-3ee4-3f58-898a-44af3ac744d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To lose interest, and start thinking about something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c26057ef-8cd8-4309-9e44-3b34967d373f",
                                                "sense_id": "78ef8052-df61-3a23-9c1b-f71536b80397",
                                                "text": "Fulham switched off as Giggs took a quick corner to Valencia. He played it back to Giggs, whose cross was headed in by Nani with the lurking Rooney unable to add a touch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38297492-e029-4e19-a311-d2348a414261",
                                                "sense_id": "78ef8052-df61-3a23-9c1b-f71536b80397",
                                                "text": "While you are pregnant with the desire for the car, the house or anything, try to switch off your mind to avoid brainstorming any solutions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73b9084d-f28d-45ed-8299-1f117aa46ad7",
                                                "sense_id": "78ef8052-df61-3a23-9c1b-f71536b80397",
                                                "text": "In short, the Bible is used by many, believers and atheists alike, as a book best handled only after switching off your brain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7eadc54a-d5ce-386e-ba89-6323ad403252",
                                        "entry_id": "a0eec63c-3ee4-3f58-898a-44af3ac744d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To alternate between; to trade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "768b04e0-7c5c-46b1-9a62-c558fe56187c",
                                                "sense_id": "7eadc54a-d5ce-386e-ba89-6323ad403252",
                                                "text": "Do you eat all your peas and then all your potatoes, or do you switch off between them as you go?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "797b01e7-abf4-4d49-a269-81f3bb58cc57",
                                                "sense_id": "7eadc54a-d5ce-386e-ba89-6323ad403252",
                                                "text": "\"We haven't a musket, and Tommy's crowd are well armed. They have the inside track\" \"Then we can switch off.\" \"Switch off?\" \"Yes, and take the inside track.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f31c58c-fb1a-4b4a-af36-0e8af01ff1dd",
                                                "sense_id": "7eadc54a-d5ce-386e-ba89-6323ad403252",
                                                "text": "Besides Crow belting out \"Bitch,\" the concert featured several artists switching off on lead vocals"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4194d6d6-19ea-444c-aa40-b1a2327971d7",
                                                "sense_id": "7eadc54a-d5ce-386e-ba89-6323ad403252",
                                                "text": "Freddie gave me a quick five-minute lesson on handling Cherry Pie and we switched off between sleeping and driving."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
